447:   private async runLanguageReflective(line: Line, stage: Stage, now: number): Promise<OrchestratorResult> {
448:     const continuityContext = this.buildContinuityContext();
449:     const contextInput = {
450:       encounter: this.encounter,
451:       significator: this.significator,
452:       holonRegistry: { holons: this.world.holons },
453:       conceptIndex: this.conceptIndex,
454:       recentConsequences: this.history,
455:       sessionContext: { energy: 'high' as const },
456:     };
457:     const context = buildContext(contextInput);
458:     const assessmentContext = this.module ? this.buildAssessmentContext(this.module) : '';
459: 
460:     const systemPrompt = `${context.systemPrompt}${assessmentContext}${continuityContext}
461: [LANGUAGE-REFLECTIVE ASSESSMENT]
462: You are conducting a deep developmental assessment through open-ended dialogue.
463: 
464: INSTRUCTIONS:
465: 1. Generate a single, profound reflective prompt that invites the player to explore their inner landscape. The prompt should be:
466:    - Stage-appropriate (Red = survival/immediate, Amber = order/belonging, Orange = achievement/autonomy, Green = connection/equity, Turquoise = systemic/integral, White = unity/transcendent)
467:    - Line-specific (Cognitive = thinking patterns, Emotional = feeling landscape, Moral = ethical reasoning, Intrapersonal = self-awareness, Spiritual = meaning/purpose, Interpersonal = relational dynamics, Somatic = body wisdom, Willpower =意志力/fortitude)
468:    - Evocative, not leading. Open a door, don't push them through it.
469: 
470: 2. Call 'ask_user_question' with EXACTLY this structure:
471:    - questions[0].question: Your evocative prompt (2-3 sentences max)
472:    - questions[0].header: "Reflection"
473:    - questions[0].options: [] (EMPTY array - no MCQ options)
474:    - questions[0].allowWriteIn: true (this is the ONLY input method)
